955	/// Autodesk FBX, binary flavour: the header is the 18 letters `Kaydara FBX
956	/// Binary`, two spaces, a NUL, then `0x1A 0x00` — 23 bytes before the uint32
957	/// version field. The three unprintable bytes are the entire discriminator;
958	/// the letters on their own are ordinary English, and they are *more* likely
959	/// to appear as prose inside this PR's own target corpus, a Unity/3D-asset
960	/// tree, than anywhere else. Measured through `sniff()`: a `.md` note opening
961	/// "Kaydara FBX Binary is the 20-byte magic that opens every binary FBX file
962	/// exported by Autodesk tools. " was `TxtProse` on `ca4d75a` and
963	/// `Binary`/`fbx` on this branch until this check existed, and `scan_file`
964	/// turns `Family::Binary` into "junk: binary content (fbx)" — never indexed.
965	fn fbx_header(prefix: &[u8]) -> bool {
966	    prefix.starts_with(b"Kaydara FBX Binary  \x00\x1a\x00")
967	}
