2807	    /// `0e5d740` and `12b4a4e` the arm was `prefix.len() >= GIF_PREFIX` alone,
2808	    /// and this paragraph read: "A cut real GIF goes to the prose extractor and
2809	    /// is sectioned into junk records — exactly the harm #379 and #427 were
2810	    /// fighting, with the sign flipped. It is preferred anyway because a
2811	    /// truncated GIF is a broken file that no decoder accepts, while the
2812	    /// alternative (answer "image" on a short buffer, round 2's rejected
2813	    /// `true`) silently drops 10 good corpus text files."
