1	//! Source adapters: turn a recipe `[[sources]]` entry into a directory to
2	//! walk, plus the upstream watermark that lets an unchanged source be
3	//! skipped wholesale on the next run.
4	//!
5	//! Kinds:
6	//! - `dir`     — walk a recipe-relative directory (the fixture/local kind)
7	//! - `http-zip`— download a zip, extract into the cache, walk the
8	//!   extraction. No watermark: the zip is re-downloaded every run and the
9	//!   content store dedups what did not change (correctness lives there,
10	//!   watermarks are only an optimization).
11	//! - `git`     — promisor shallow checkout at `rev` (pinned) or the remote
12	//!   HEAD (tracking). Watermark = HEAD sha: unchanged tree ⇒ the walk is
13	//!   skipped entirely this run.
14	//!
15	//! Zip extraction is defensive by default: entry names are normalized and
16	//! any path escaping the extraction root (zip-slip), absolute path, or
17	//! symlink entry is skipped and COUNTED, never trusted — dump URLs are
18	//! fetched from the open internet.
